---
title: Chicken Sausage, Brussels Sprouts and White Beans
source: claude
servings: 4
tags: [freezer, sheet-pan]
cook time: 25-35 minutes
---

> About 9 g fiber and 28 g protein per serving. If frozen, thaw before roasting.

Heat the oven to 425°F.

Toss @chicken sausage{1%lb}(fully cooked, sliced), @brussels sprouts{1%lb}(halved), @cannellini beans{15%oz}(drained) and @red onion{1}(cut into wedges) with @olive oil{2%tbsp}, @dijon mustard{1%tbsp} and @garlic powder{1%tsp}.

Spread on a #sheet pan{} and roast for ~{25-35%minutes}, until the sprouts are tender and browned.
